}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})=y{e}^{xy}, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})=x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186434987 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434987 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434987 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7054d950-8f37-587d-a33e-968d65e47cb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434988 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434988 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434988 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7643073f-ce44-57df-9282-30a16459d53b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434991 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434991 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434991 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7f059d2-e77c-5931-aa43-e92b03f2ab7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434993 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf609f5e-73ea-5693-ba97-16c620f066fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434994 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3ddf159-b8c5-5358-82de-10f08389dfb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434995 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "be799441-b520-5409-95fd-e9decc4e3407" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163077" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1),\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df9f8fb7-c1aa-51d4-afc9-10cbbb747f39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434998 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1} & \\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+(-\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{2}{3}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442211 #edb/ref 1044 #edb